  <h2>A worked human route to the same path</h2>

  <p>
    The manual route stopped being hypothetical on 1 August 2026, when
    bitcoin++ Insider Edition published
    <a href="/record/sources/btcpp-dettmer-commit-history/">Dustin Dettmer's commit-history walkthrough</a>.
    Working from the public repository, it reaches the board override, the
    disabled macro and the symbol the seed path actually calls, and it credits
    no model assistance.
    <Claim
      basis="verified"
      scope="That a published post-disclosure analysis reconstructs the faulty path from commit history without claimed model assistance"
      source="Dettmer's analysis as captured, with its commit-level claims separately checked against the pinned firmware clones"
      href="/record/sources/btcpp-dettmer-commit-history/"
      compact
    />
    This archive checked its commit-level assertions
    against the pinned clones and found most of them exact, one dating claim
    unsupported and one cited commit not locatable; the full check is on
    <a href="/response/developers/#commit-history">the developer-response page</a>.
    <Claim
      basis="unverified"
      scope="Whether the original finder used a comparable manual route"
      source="A demonstrated post-disclosure route does not evidence the pre-disclosure one; no discovery artefact has been captured"
      compact
    />
  </p>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--blue">
    <div class="ve-card__label lbl-blue">What would change the status</div>
    <p>
      A contemporaneous transcript, model identifier, dated analysis or account
      from the original finder could support the discovery claim. Until such
      evidence appears, the appropriate status is <strong>unverified</strong>.
      <Claim
        basis="unverified"
        scope="The method by which the attacker or original discoverer found the vulnerable path"
        source="Coinkite's stated inference; no public discovery artefact in the captured record"
        compact
      />
    </p>
  </div>
</Article>
